^SAMPLE = GSM7089855
!Sample_title = Visium result of patient 1
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM7089855
!Sample_status = Public on Mar 14 2023
!Sample_submission_date = Mar 09 2023
!Sample_last_update_date = Mar 15 2023
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Primary colorectal cancer
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: Human colorectal cancer
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = Sex: Female
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = t staging: 3
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = n staging: N0
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = m staging: M0
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Colorectal cancer tissues were collected under the protocol of Review Board at Ajou University Hospital (AJOUIRB-OBS-2016-218).  Then the tissues were processed into formalin-fixed paraffin-embedded (FFPE) samples
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Two sections per patients were cut at 10 mm thickness. One is mounted onto Visium slide capture area, and the other is used for hematoxyllin & eosin staining. Sequencing libraries were prepared following the manufacturer's protocol. After tissue staining, bright-field images were taken as described in the Spatial Transcriptomics procedure. The Visium Spatial Gene Expression Slide & Reacgent kit (10X genomics) was used to make sequencing libraries.
!Sample_data_processing = For Visium, libraries were sequenced on a NextSeq (Illumina), with 28 bases from read 1 and 120 from read 2, and at a depth of 84-116 million reads per sample. Following demultiplexing of bcl files, the read 2 fastq files were trimmed using Cutadapt (Martin, 2011) (Martin, 2011) to remove full-length or truncated template switch oligo (TSO) sequences from the 5’ end and polyA homopolymers from the 3’ end. The TSO sequence ( AAGCAGTGGTATCAACGCAGAGTACATGGG) was used as a non-internal 5’ adapter with a minimum overlap of 5, meaning that partial matches (up to 5 base pairs) or intact TSO sequences were removed from the 5’ end of read 2. The error tolerance was set to 0.1 for the TSO trimming to allow for a maximum of 3 errors. For the 3’ homopolymer trimming, a sequence of 10 As was used as a regular 3’ adapter to remove potential polyA tail products regardless of its position in the read, also with a minimum overlap of 5 base pairs. The trimmed data was processed with the spaceranger pipeline (version 1.0.0, 10X Genomics) and mapped to the GRCH38 v93 genome assembly.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: GRCh38 v86
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: barcodes.tsv, features.tsv, and matrix.mtx
!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: Spatial transcriptomics
!Sample_platform_id = GPL30173
!Sample_contact_name = Soon Sang,,Park
!Sample_contact_email = sspark9395@ajou.ac.kr
!Sample_contact_institute = Ajou University School of Medicine
!Sample_contact_address = Worldcup-Ro 206
!Sample_contact_city = Suwon
!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 16499
!Sample_contact_country = South Korea
!Sample_instrument_model = NextSeq 2000
!Sample_library_selection = other
!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic
!Sample_library_strategy = OTHER
!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN33698434
!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX19610993
!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM7089nnn/GSM7089855/suppl/GSM7089855_Ajou_Visium_P1.tar.gz
!Sample_series_id = GSE226997
!Sample_data_row_count = 0
